{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/611354-greater-elemental-dragons-and-why","id":611354,"title":"Greater Elemental Dragons and Why","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-01T14:40:03-07:00","id":611354,"title":"Greater Elemental Dragons and Why","content":"So I've been thinking about the old problem of why do Elemental Dragons go crazy. It never really made sense to me. E9 perfectly fine functioning lesser dragon, E10 bam raging godzilla like greater elemental dragon. Looking through the Infernals bit and saw the part with Hellstriders and Limit, specifically the sidebar about supernumerary demons and permanent limit and it clicked.<br /> <br /> Greater Elemental Dragons have a permanent Limit of 10.<br /> <br /> Some of you may be thinking duh, or now that you mention it... what can I say... I got nothing.<br /> <br /> But! But! Something in the transformation causes the limit gain. Or maybe they are just rapidly accruing limit and are continuously limit breaking so that it appears like it is permanent.<br /> <br /> But then you have motherfunkers like Gardullis is just sit there in quiescence ruining the train. Maybe just Kukla went crazy... except it says that they all go crazy.<br /> <br /> So what do you think? Agree/Disagree? Any thoughts as to what the Limit conditions might be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T16:03:35-07:00","id":611427,"title":"","content":"I never really thought of it as them going insane. I prefer to think of it that a Greater Elemental Dragon is just very, very, VERY powerful. Like, a Greater Wind Dragon just breathing would cause a hurricane. It's like when you're a human and you're walking across the ground when there's some ants. Doesn't matter if you try to be careful, sooner or later you're going to crush some ants.<br /> <br /> Nothing personal to the ants. You just didn't see them there.<br /> <br /> So Kukla can't help but cause earthquakes, that's just part of its nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T16:49:46-07:00","id":611461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tenkage</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then you have motherfunkers like Gardullis is just sit there in quiescence ruining the train. Maybe just Kukla went crazy... except it says that they all go crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah yes, the Gardullis sitting in quiescence, as opposed to the Kukla who is sitting in quiescence inside a volcano at the bottom of the ocean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T16:53:05-07:00","id":611462,"title":"","content":"I think Limit and the Limit track is intended to be an abstraction, not a discernible in-setting Thing.<br /> <br /> There's also something weird there, since Limit (IIRC) is inherently tied to the Great Curse and/or being Exalted, not to elementals. Unless there's something with Cselinine pacts I'm forgetting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T17:06:56-07:00","id":611478,"title":"","content":"Anyway, the distinction is a bit arbitrary, isn't it? It makes no sense for them to suddenly go crazy, but it makes perfect sense for them to suddenly accumulate enough Limit to go crazy? Are they not basically the same thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T17:25:04-07:00","id":611488,"title":"","content":"I don't think sanity or insanity are useful ways of discussing Greater Elemental Dragons. Is a hurricane mad? Can a volcano practice rationality?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T17:35:20-07:00","id":611497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also something weird there, since Limit (IIRC) is inherently tied to the Great Curse and/or being Exalted, not to elementals. Unless there's something with Cselinine pacts I'm forgetting.</div> </div> </div> </div> I can't recall how it's portrayed with elementals, but I know that demons adapt the Limit concept to represent the idea of mounting psychological pressure from orders or context contradicting their maniacal pursuits or idiosyncratic attitudes (especially when Absicissic binding is used to break their personalities into more manageable forms). An example is hopping puppeteers, who are extremely restless, gain Limit from any attempt to keep them immobile, either through orders or physical restraint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T17:38:00-07:00","id":611499,"title":"","content":"I've always felt that the reason Elementsl Dragons go full Kukla when they hit Essence: 10 was related to the Primordials' destruction of the original Great Elementals in the early part of the Primordial War.<br /> <br /> Some background, not often mentioned since 1st Ed.: the Incarnae, inspired by Gaia's Five Elemental Dragon offspring, created the Great Elementals as one of their first autonomous acts after the Primordials gave them the keys to Creation and told them to start running it. Oceku, Urwl, Mindful Forest, the Wind Master, and the Great Garda were pretty much the only elementals in existence, and had commensurately great power; the Great Garda, for example, was powerful and organized enough to be in charge of all fires everywhere, both terrestrially and celestially. <br /> <br /> When the gods first rebelled, the Primordials responded in predictable fashion: They looked at what the gods had made, and smashed it to bits. By annihilating the five super elementals, not only did they remove a powerful weapon that could be used against them, they put Creation into a serious tailspin, forcing the Incarnae and the gods to patch things up, instead of fighting. With the Exalted to press the war though, the gods were able to perform some emergency repairs.<br /> <br /> The immense amounts of Essence the Incarnae had invested in the Great Elementals had been scattered, coalescing into lesser gods whose form and function reflected some aspect of the being it had previously belonged to. In damage control mode, Gaia sent the Five Elemental Dragons to wrangle these disparate lesser gods into line, creating the first Elemental Courts. Over time, dribs and drabs of OG Elemental Essence sprouted into lesser elementals, whose late arrival and often low intelligence contributed to the bigoted attitudes about them that still persist.<br /> <br /> SO! I think that when a Lesser Elemental Dragon reaches the pinnacle of enlightenment (Essence: 10), it suddenly realizes the commonality of sentience that its element once had. When the Kukla hit Ess. 10, its insight evolved to the point where it understood and perceived all earth as one being, drawing upon the power of all earth at the same instant that it attempted to reassemble the mind common to all earth, the mind of Urwl. But since the Essence and duties of Urwl were now spread amongst nigh-infinite numbers of Gemlords, Terraserpents, Mercury Ant hives, Kri, Jokun, etc, attempting to encompass all those minds was impossible, even at the Kukla's vastly increased level of power. His sentience shattered, and he became Creation's doomsday device/reset button.<br /> <br /> Tl; dr: When Lesser Elemental Dragons hit Ess: 10, they tap into the might and mind of the first Great Elementals. Since the Great Elementals only exist as all the lesser elementals nowadays, tapping into their minds drives them super-crazy, even as they become super-powerful.<br /> <br /> ETA: crossposting this to the headcanon thread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1536-39steps","user":"39Steps","date":". 08-01-2015, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1536-39steps","name":"39Steps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T19:06:46-07:00","id":611632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think sanity or insanity are useful ways of discussing Greater Elemental Dragons. Is a hurricane mad? Can a volcano practice rationality?</div> </div> </div> </div> At the very least, I think it's reasonably apt to convey the idea of what the transition of somebody like Fakharu would look like to everybody else. Whether or not he <u>is</u> mad is not as significant as the fact that he <u>is not</u> interested in art, history or his lover anymore. That (and the entire premise of the thread) does of course rely on the assumption that the Kukla was ever a person like Fakharu, which is not directly stated in the previewed elemental section, nor was it part of the original write-up in Games of Divinity. Really, even if he was, I'm not sure if a depiction that directly acted as though the change was some form of debilitation was present before Compass: Yu-Shan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T19:08:57-07:00","id":611635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/611354-greater-elemental-dragons-and-why?p=611632#post611632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> At the very least, I think it's reasonably apt to convey the idea of what the transition of somebody like Fakharu would look like to everybody else. Whether or not he <u>is</u> mad is not as significant as the fact that he <u>is not</u> interested in art, history or his lover anymore. That (and the entire premise of the thread) does of course rely on the assumption that the Kukla was ever a person like Fakharu, which is not directly stated in the previewed elemental section, nor was it part of the original write-up in Games of Divinity. Really, even if he was, I'm not sure if a depiction that directly acted as though the change was some form of debilitation was present before Compass: Yu-Shan.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lesser elemental dragon who ascends to become a greater elemental dragon doesn't &quot;go mad&quot; so much as they cease to be a person, becoming instead an incarnate force of nature. None of the everyday examples of madness are really useful for analogizing that transition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T19:36:37-07:00","id":611666,"title":"","content":"Quiescence as compared to Kukla is bound and sleeping where as Gardullis is a watchful guardian aboard the Daystar that can apparently function as the watchdog of the Aidenweiss whereas Kukla can only SMASH!<br /> <br /> Is a Hurricane or Earthquake insane? No. Is the God of Earthquakes or Hurricanes insane? Possibly. Sanity is always relative but generally when a force has some basis of valid personification, it is not surprising that one would judge it via the same standards of sapience for those like it. Now if you're saying becoming a GED destroys their Sapience, that Kukla isn't Kukla but is the Greater Elemental Dragon of Earth formerly known as Kukla... well that would make sanity a moot point. I don't like that.<br /> <br /> As for 39steps' idea, I like that interpretation quite a bit. It makes sense.<br /> <br /> Because beneath it all, the rational mind of Kukla DOES exist. And can be restored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T19:39:43-07:00","id":611672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tenkage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/611354-greater-elemental-dragons-and-why?p=611666#post611666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is a Hurricane or Earthquake insane? No. Is the God of Earthquakes or Hurricanes insane? Possibly. Sanity is always relative but generally when a force has some basis of valid personification, it is not surprising that one would judge it via the same standards of sapience for those like it. Now if you're saying becoming a GED destroys their Sapience, that Kukla isn't Kukla but is the Greater Elemental Dragon of Earth formerly known as Kukla... well that would make sanity a moot point. I don't like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it destroys the person they were. I think it expands it beyond the boundaries of what a person is. The Kukla is the Kukla is the Kukla. He's* just become something bigger and beyond what he once was. <br /> <br /> *or she? I can't remember the Kukla's pronouns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T19:41:06-07:00","id":611674,"title":"","content":"The idea that it would mean something of significance to elementals certainly does strike me as a more palatable reason for ones to have pursued the ascension after the Kukla than &quot;they did the exact same thing expecting a different outcome&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T19:55:55-07:00","id":611705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/611354-greater-elemental-dragons-and-why?p=611672#post611672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He\u2026 or she? I can't remember the Kukla's pronouns.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Kukla identifies as the Kukla. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/611354-greater-elemental-dragons-and-why?p=611672#post611672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kukla is the Kukla is the Kukla.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T21:21:47-07:00","id":611846,"title":"","content":"This is kind of the essence of transcendence, here, where you cast off mortal aspersions and become something 'more.'<br /> <br /> People with a human-esque perception can kind of grapple with such a consciousness, but they're crude linguistic best-fits; Malfeas &quot;rages,&quot; Cecelyne &quot;covets,&quot; the Kukla &quot;sleeps&quot;... or how about God &quot;loves&quot;?<br /> <br /> But in order for it to not seem, frankly, entirely insane in human terms you'd have to slough off this crude matter and transcend yourself.<br /> <br /> At which point, to your former elemental colleagues, you would seem <i>crazy</i>. There's a reason Gaia told Hesiesh and Pasiap to take a power-nap; primal, transcendent expressions of Earth and Fire are pretty inimical to the lives of those pink hairless apes that deem themselves masters of Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T22:00:07-07:00","id":611887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/611354-greater-elemental-dragons-and-why?p=611488#post611488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think sanity or insanity are useful ways of discussing Greater Elemental Dragons. Is a hurricane mad? Can a volcano practice rationality?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, volcanoes and hurricanes aren't even alive, so it absolutely would be wrong to say that they're &quot;insane.&quot; I guess would it be better to say that Greater Elemental Dragons aren't sentient and are therefore mindless (in the most literal sense) forces of elemental power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T00:07:49-07:00","id":611945,"title":"","content":"I have always thought that what happened was that some writer read the &quot;lesser elemental dragon&quot; entry in the core book and thought this meant that there were greater elemental dragons instead of realizing that they were &quot;lesser&quot; elemental dragons because the Five Elemental Dragons were already a thing. Of course, why these greater elemental dragons aren't doing things when their lesser kin are had to be explained, resulting in the Godzilla problem.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think this could all be fixed by having some &quot;lesser elemental dragons&quot; like the Kukla who are incarnate forces of nature while others are working as celestial functionaries or claiming their own spirit court. Then we don't have to think about Essence 10 as an important thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T01:23:08-07:00","id":611963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/611354-greater-elemental-dragons-and-why?p=611705#post611705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kukla identifies as the Kukla.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.schlockmercenary.com/2008-07-24\" target=\"_blank\">Kukla is too large for your puny pronouns.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","user":"Dusk Shine","date":". 08-02-2015, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T01:33:10-07:00","id":611964,"title":"","content":"I have never found the &quot;too great and vast for your tiny human perceptions&quot; a particularly helpful handwave, because any attempt to write them is a human mind writing them. The Unconquered Sun himself is, at least to a degree, sapient in the normal way, otherwise how does he communicate with this Zeniths? Are we now to say that the Kukla possesses perceptions more vast, or a greater mind?<br /> <br /> Saying 'Kukla's being cannot be comprehended&quot; feels cheap. If we want to think of GEDs as hurricanes, or volcanoes, then we need to essentially cross &quot;sapient&quot; off the list. Which is cool with me. Saying that there are certain forces in Creation that just <i>are</i>, that will wreak terrible destruction, and must sleep, is very evocative.<br /> <br /> I don't see it as 100% necessary though, especially in a game with a much smaller focus than 2nd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T02:43:05-07:00","id":611980,"title":"","content":"Yeah I dunno, I don't think &quot;it's sufficiently 'bigger' than you that any approximation of its psychology will be just that, an approximation&quot; is quite the same thing. You can't sit the Kukla down for a cup of tea while you discuss that whole &quot;ending all currently-existing life, destroying all the shadowlands and setting the slate blank again&quot; thing. Doesn't mean you can't attempt to comprehend it, it's just, why it's rampaging will never really make &quot;sense&quot; to you because you're not &quot;big&quot; enough, and your concerns about pink fleshy things will never really make &quot;sense&quot; to it because it's not &quot;small&quot; enough.<br /> <br /> Except for that one smutfic where somebody's lunar mate got it on with the Kukla. <i>That</i> was probably talking on its level.<br /> <br /> I think the fact that Gardulis is content to be the flame of the greatest forge that ever was, and Kukla would destroy the world given the chance to roam free... they're both &quot;crazy,&quot; it's just that people conflate &quot;crazy&quot; with &quot;violent&quot; with &quot;omnicidal&quot; like they have to go together, which is... rather unfortunate leap of logic. The Maidens are &quot;crazy&quot; too, and for that matter, so is Luna! They're just human-shaped when they want to be so people give them a bye like they aren't some kind of inhuman monsters. (Also, you <i>can</i> sit them down for tea, and they'll probably listen.)<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun is an engine of nigh-infinite divine fire too strong and too hot for Creation to actually bear. Yes, I would actually say he possesses a greater mind with vaster perceptions (and perceptions largely orthogonal to human ones) than most people, even most Solars, would be capable of. But I mean, even Solars can get to see the building blocks of what makes a person animate (at Essence 2, no less) or how compassionate they are or how far they'll go for their goals just by looking at 'em.<br /> <br /> Heck, &quot;that villain is crazy&quot; is a stupid narrative kludge to fit any of their behavior into the confines of the story, but there's a wide gulf between &quot;that villain's motives cannot be comprehended&quot; and &quot;that villain's priorities are deeply alien.&quot; You want Cenobites from the first couple of Hellraiser movies, as mad alien sensates, not the later sequels where they just murdered everyone.<br /> <br /> You want a method to the madness, the Kukla as a world-destroying fishmalk is... kind of hilarious but no good for anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 08-02-2015, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T03:28:11-07:00","id":612014,"title":"","content":"I really don't think the Kukla needs to be more elaborate than &quot;gigantic dragon sleeping beneath the Earth whose movement unleashes disasters&quot;. If lesser elemental dragons weren't around I doubt it would even be an issue, but as it is the idea that one can graduate from that state into cosmological myth dragon doesn't seem like it should be very complicated. Maybe even more so, with the changes to elementals; I could extend my idea of elementals as candidates for forces utilized in the making of Creation to the notion that the height of their power is a return to that primal state, an approximation of the crucible in which a world is formed. The Kukla as an embodiment of the Earth in its depths, in its youth, churning with eruptions, the clashes that raise mountains. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have never found the &quot;too great and vast for your tiny human perceptions&quot; a particularly helpful handwave, because any attempt to write them is a human mind writing them.</div> </div> </div> </div> You cheat by skirting around the edges. Same as any character, really; you can't ever actually comprehensively model a complex, three-dimensional person, but you can create a lot of images that trick people into thinking that it is. Or a lot of animals for that matter, especially when you've got Lunars turning into them; imagine seeing through the eyes of a mantis shrimp, and then realise that you can't because how can you comprehend colours that don't even fit within the range of your vision. How do you play a Lunar in that shape?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T03:28:21-07:00","id":612016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/611354-greater-elemental-dragons-and-why?p=611980#post611980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &lt;snip&gt;<br /> <br /> I think the fact that Gardulis is content to be the flame of the greatest forge that ever was, and Kukla would destroy the world given the chance to roam free... they're both &quot;crazy,&quot; it's just that people conflate &quot;crazy&quot; with &quot;violent&quot; with &quot;omnicidal&quot; like they have to go together, which is... rather unfortunate leap of logic. The Maidens are &quot;crazy&quot; too, and for that matter, so is Luna! They're just human-shaped when they want to be so people give them a bye like they aren't some kind of inhuman monsters. (Also, you <i>can</i> sit them down for tea, and they'll probably listen.)<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun is an engine of nigh-infinite divine fire too strong and too hot for Creation to actually bear. Yes, I would actually say he possesses a greater mind with vaster perceptions (and perceptions largely orthogonal to human ones) than most people, even most Solars, would be capable of. But I mean, even Solars can get to see the building blocks of what makes a person animate (at Essence 2, no less) or how compassionate they are or how far they'll go for their goals just by looking at 'em.<br /> <br /> Heck, &quot;that villain is crazy&quot; is a stupid narrative kludge to fit any of their behavior into the confines of the story, but there's a wide gulf between &quot;that villain's motives cannot be comprehended&quot; and &quot;that villain's priorities are deeply alien.&quot; You want Cenobites from the first couple of Hellraiser movies, as mad alien sensates, not the later sequels where they just murdered everyone.<br /> <br /> You want a method to the madness, the Kukla as a world-destroying fishmalk is... kind of hilarious but no good for anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet, the Incarnae, and most gods in general, are intended to be understandable by humans, and the gods are supposed to have relations with humans. So, while their perceptions and thoughts are different, they are sufficiently similar that they are useful to the story. Sol narratively, is derived from gods like Zeus, not gods like Cthulu. There is a conceit in mythology that says these incredibly powerful beings give a shit about little ole' us, and that we can actually deal with them, and even outsmart them or defeat them, at least for a time. Those myths are drawn upon heavily by Exalted.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Kukla is not a fishmalk; that ruins the whole thing. If he's more like a hurricane, or a super-volcano, an urge more than a person, then we are actually filling useful narrative space. The Kukla is not an enemy. The Kukla is not an ally. The Kukla is a giant plot device of doom.<br /> <br /> Also, this conversation may be moot. I can't see much use to the devs in delving too deep into the GED end of things in a game largely centered on crumbling empires and desperate struggles for mortal power.<br /> <br /> I do think &quot;crazy&quot; is tossed around a bit too much to justify evil. Course, Exalted leans on it pretty heavily (*looks at the Great Curse*).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T04:01:55-07:00","id":612024,"title":"","content":"I think gods should be comparable to humans in some broad strokes of their personality, emotional spectrum and relationships with one another (and the relatively small number of humans whom they wind up relating to), but are often attached to people in a general, abstract sense, can emotionally value a lot of things more than they do people, aren't necessarily interested in cultivating relationships or being part of a community or absorbing culture, and just don't get a lot of human needs and impulses.<br /> <br /> Like, hardly any god has ever known hunger, even in the sense of the slight discomfort you feel when you've been too long between meals; that's a pretty serious departure from all humans, even the Exalted, right there (I don't think there's ever been a Resistance or Survival Charm published that helps with the issue of starving or dehydrating to death, as opposed to gathering food, and while it certainly fits within the range of what a Solar could achieve there are going to be a lot of players and characters who wouldn't bother with such a thing, so... good luck getting stuck in a barren cave).<br /> <br /> Speaking of caves, consider the idea of a Solar who goes deep into one that nobody else has ever been in; if you encounter one of the native spirits of echos and darkness, he might have a form that very vaguely resembles you, will speak in a language that you can know (and probably with a dialect that is at least barely comprehensible), and might have some of the personality of a crotchety hermit who hates intrusions and company, but he's also a thing that has lived with contentment in the darkness for a million years, with a set of internal needs that is fulfilled by what could be found in such a place and a perception that sees what is around them in the necessary terms, and it's like... how do you relate to that? How does it relate to you? It's really really outside the range of anybody's experience.<br /> <br /> You can talk to each other but, well, you can always talk to somebody who has experienced something so far outside the range of your own life that you just can't truly internalise or model what the experience of it really is, and depending on the people that difference can form a barrier against any form of more sophisticated relationship.<br /> <br /> Also depends on how one thinks the powers gods have to be aware of their purview and domains works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T04:25:09-07:00","id":612036,"title":"","content":"Isator: Abyssal Resistance. AFB at the moment but I think it's called &quot;Corpse Needs No Food.&quot; You can even take it as a Taint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T04:34:28-07:00","id":612040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/611354-greater-elemental-dragons-and-why?p=612024#post612024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think gods should be comparable to humans in some broad strokes of their personality, emotional spectrum and relationships with one another (and the relatively small number of humans whom they wind up relating to), but are often attached to people in a general, abstract sense, can emotionally value a lot of things more than they do people, aren't necessarily interested in cultivating relationships or being part of a community or absorbing culture, and just don't get a lot of human needs and impulses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am reminded of the Godblooded chapter fiction from the First Edition Player's Handbook.<br /> <br /> That said, I think most gods should ultimately be fairly relate-able to humanity (if a bit quirky) and relatively easy for PC's to interact with. Yeah, they'll be a little strange - so will Dragon Kings and Ghosts and Fair Folk and Demons and even Beastmen. But only truly edge cases (like Greater Elemental Dragons or truly bizarre behemoths or demons) should be beyond comprehension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 08-02-2015, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T05:26:35-07:00","id":612097,"title":"","content":"I meant <i>Solar</i> Charm. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I think most gods should ultimately be fairly relate-able to humanity (if a bit quirky) and relatively easy for PC's to interact with.</div> </div> </div> </div> That was what I was trying to get at, yes. For the most part conversation will be fairly normal, but every now and then it will be sprinkled with something like frantically asking what time it is and having the god of a hill or something reply &quot;night... time?&quot; (This is just an example, I know most people in Creation won't be tracking time according to the hour and minute)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T05:31:23-07:00","id":612102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/611354-greater-elemental-dragons-and-why?p=611635#post611635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lesser elemental dragon who ascends to become a greater elemental dragon doesn't &amp;quot;go mad&amp;quot; so much as they cease to be a person, becoming instead an incarnate force of nature. None of the everyday examples of madness are really useful for analogizing that transition.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I saw it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/687-cydoc","name":"Cydoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T08:42:32-07:00","id":612269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/611354-greater-elemental-dragons-and-why?p=611945#post611945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always thought that what happened was that some writer read the &quot;lesser elemental dragon&quot; entry in the core book and thought this meant that there were greater elemental dragons instead of realizing that they were &quot;lesser&quot; elemental dragons because the Five Elemental Dragons were already a thing. Of course, why these greater elemental dragons aren't doing things when their lesser kin are had to be explained, resulting in the Godzilla problem.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think this could all be fixed by having some &quot;lesser elemental dragons&quot; like the Kukla who are incarnate forces of nature while others are working as celestial functionaries or claiming their own spirit court. Then we don't have to think about Essence 10 as an important thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So your take on it is that Kukla was always meant to be Godzilla? That's how he was out the door?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T08:55:03-07:00","id":612294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/611354-greater-elemental-dragons-and-why?p=612269#post612269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So your take on it is that Kukla was always meant to be Godzilla? That's how he was out the door?</div> </div> </div> </div>Has anyone taken a picture of Godzilla and the Kukla in the same place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T09:12:04-07:00","id":612315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/611354-greater-elemental-dragons-and-why?p=611945#post611945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always thought that what happened was that some writer read the &quot;lesser elemental dragon&quot; entry in the core book and thought this meant that there were greater elemental dragons instead of realizing that they were &quot;lesser&quot; elemental dragons because the Five Elemental Dragons were already a thing. Of course, why these greater elemental dragons aren't doing things when their lesser kin are had to be explained, resulting in the Godzilla problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having looked up Fakharu recently (and re-checked now), the 1e corebook clearly mentions elemental dragons who are &quot;ravening coils of elemental fury&quot; sealed Elsewhere or set to guard holy places, but it doesn't specify that they are <i>Greater</i>, just dragons in contrast to the likes of the censors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T09:48:10-07:00","id":612338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/611354-greater-elemental-dragons-and-why?p=611945#post611945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always thought that what happened was that some writer read the &quot;lesser elemental dragon&quot; entry in the core book and thought this meant that there were greater elemental dragons instead of realizing that they were &quot;lesser&quot; elemental dragons because the Five Elemental Dragons were already a thing. Of course, why these greater elemental dragons aren't doing things when their lesser kin are had to be explained, resulting in the Godzilla problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the Kukla was called out in Games of Divinity as a Greater Elemental Dragon, and that was still very early on the gameline (GoD was only published a year after the release of the corebook). It seems more likely that Grabowski approved of the idea than not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T14:47:10-07:00","id":612618,"title":"","content":"I always kind of thought of Greater Elemental Dragons as being like Dr. Manhattan. He didn't go crazy, he just became alien.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T16:26:45-07:00","id":612777,"title":"","content":"Re: communication with transcendent gods, having a more expansive form of awareness is pretty different from communication. Some gods have a larger awareness than humans and feel like talking. Some don't.<br /> <br /> Kulka's seems more like the latter, the UCS is occasionally the former. More of what the UCS would say could be fit into magically enhanced human language, while the Kulka's perceptions, maybe not. Could words really express what it experiences? Or can they only &quot;hint&quot; at them, much like Isator is suggesting is the good strategy to writing a character like Kulka?<br /> <br /> Gods in Exalted are both genuinely transcendent and divine and genuinely petty, at the same time. They're inspired by Dunsany, after all, for all that the tone of Exalted books is more prose, less poetry (and other differences in outlook and focus). They derive from The Gods of Pegana, as much as or more than from the images of Zeus or Apollo as modern people think of them (and of course, the likes of the Kami of Shinto are pretty important as well). And of course, this is in sort of in keeping with contrasts of cholera and glorious demigods fighting for love. You kind of want to keep that up and not collapse it into &quot;They're like us, or they're cosmic idiots whose different perspective is fundamentally a kind of limitation and insanity, rather than a kind of divinity&quot; (although that's always been more a forum thing that a books thing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T23:36:31-07:00","id":613053,"title":"","content":"Or could it be that Creation is so wounded that when awake Kukla can sense nothing but the overwhelming need to fix it with such intensity it can only appear to us mere mortals and the August Assemblage of Heaven naught but madness and destruction even as life flourishes in his wake?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T10:49:58-07:00","id":616667,"title":"","content":"The weird thing is, if we take some of the later rules written up on the Garduulis into account...it is still sapient enough to follow orders. The write-up on the Daystar was deemed 2.5 canon, and included an explanation that the Garduulis could and would be deployed to recover Aidenweiss should it be stolen from its rightful place. This implies that it is intelligent enough, and sane enough, to follow orders. &quot;Go get the superweapon sword and bring it back.&quot;<br /> <br /> The problem is...the Garduulis is flame incarnate and is miles long. There's going to be collateral damage.<br /> <br /> According to the 2E Lore...elementals evolve as they grow more powerful. They start off as representations of their element...then they become a quite large dragon...then they become an apocalypse dragon. When these transitions occur, their personalities and behaviors change. The thing to remember, IMO, is that they are not gods, and they do not work like gods. Where gods becomes progressively more powerful and intelligent as they gain Essence, elementals seem to change in fits and starts. Like a god, they start off as something basically unaware of its surroundings. A mere manifestation of its element. They gradually become more intelligent and more powerful as they gain Essence and up to this point, look a lot like the development of a god.<br /> <br /> Then they hit the Essence necessary for dragonization. They explode upward in size and intelligence, becoming a Lesser Elemental Dragon and leap above the 'second class citizen' status that normal elementals have. Then they sort of plateau for a while...they continue to gain power and the like...until they hit Essence 10. When that happens, the change that overtakes them is just as dramatic. Again, they explode upward in size, becoming something incredibly vast and apocalyptically powerful. And, to the appearance of pretty much everyone else, they go utterly insane.<br /> <br /> But....the Garduulis sleeps within the sun. The Kukla sleeps beneath the waves, awaiting its appointed time to destroy the world. The Garduulis is obedient to TUS on its instructions to safeguard Aidenweiss. So, they can't be utterly unreasoning monsters. But, again, elementals are not like gods...they don't work the same way gods do, so there is no reason to expect their spiritual growth to work the way a god's does. Here are some options, IMO, that explain their seeming madness.<br /> <br /> 1: Their Mental state changes again, turning them into a true manifestation of their element. Like how an Alchemical with High Clarity becomes machine-like and unrelatable by normal people, a Greater Elemental Dragon becomes element-like and so no longer makes sense to anyone who is not like that element. Their destructive tendencies can be explained pretty well this way. The Elemental Poles spread their influence throughout the world...now you have a miles long ambulatory manifestation of that element...it intends to spread its influence throughout the world, remaking it in the image of its element. They are basically gargantuan terraforming engines...it just sucks to be in the way of their terraforming efforts. However, as they are not completely lost to the rest of the world (just like a high-Clarity Alchemical can still be talked to and interacted with), a sufficiently powerful being, with the right persuasions, can convince them to hold back from their newfound urge to terraform Creation. This is why they sleep...the scraps of relatability left in them were enough to convince them to resist their urge to spread their element, and the easiest way for them to resist it was to hibernate.<br /> <br /> 2: They aren't actually insane. They are completely sane, and totally aware of the ramifications of what happens if they go out and play. Their power is such that their mere presence causes disruption of Essence lines because of the massive elemental flux that they generate, and this results in disasters related to their element. The currently existing GEDs voluntarily entered hibernation, and allowed the misinformation about their madness to be spread in order to prevent further disasters from occurring if more GEDs were born. The maidens prophesied that one day, their unbridled destruction would become necessary....and so they sleep, awaiting that dreadful day when they are to be awakened and must again witness the immense destruction that they cause. The misinformation plot was coined by Luna and enforced by the Maidens, and is persisted as a way to convince LEDs to not attempt to ascend to GED status as a form of damage control to protect Creation. It is possible that the other Incarna voluntarily allowed Jupiter to seal their memories to protect this secret. (Imagine what would happen if there were 50 Kuklas, even if they were all sane.)<br /> <br /> 3: Intentional Sabotage. This one goes out to all the players and STs who like to paint the Incarna as significantly less sympathetic. The Incarna realized that a combined host of Greater Elemental Dragons may be enough to cast them down. After all, they themselves orchestrated the coup against the Primordials, who treated them as second class citizens. Just to be safe, they ensured that a coordinated host of Greater Elemental Dragons could not happen. Perhaps not all of the Incarna are in on it...but at least Jupiter would need to be, and maybe Saturn as well. So, they altered the Fate of elementals such that when they struck Essence 10 and Ascended...their sanity would be terminated. In this case, they are little more than wild dogs that can be aimed at the right thing and unleashed if necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T15:07:02-07:00","id":616830,"title":"","content":"I think the Gardullis was supposed to be bound by some kind of magic rather than following a kind of order. I mean, to the extent that a capacity to follow orders implies intelligence or a coherent mind; hopping puppeteers can do it and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T10:02:01-07:00","id":617837,"title":"","content":"There are other references about this political situation the Greater Elemental Dragons?<br /> <br /> &quot;When, soon afterwards, the lesser elemental dragon of earth called the Kukla (see pp. 102-103) blossomed further and became a huge miles-long beast, the Five Elemental Dragons were well pleased their forms were so well represented in the emergent properties of elemental Essence. Soon, other dragons mimicked the Kukla\u2019s metamorphosis. Though the Five Elemental Dragons were overjoyed to see such tributes to their majesty, the gods of Yu-Shan worried. These greater elemental dragons possessed power untested and seemed mightier even than many demons of the Third Circle. The Incarnae bound the greater elemental dragons to remote places and duties so as to prevent their free reign across Creation.&quot; [BoS, vol. 4, pg. 74]<br /> <br /> &quot;Expanding to over four miles long, the Kukla\u2019s mind seemed burned away by the transformation, leaving only devastating elemental rage. The ruin left in the Kukla\u2019s wake posed significant problems to the Solar Deliberative, and Anisa-Shoshan contacted the most venerable Zenith caste priests and persuaded them to pray to the Unconquered Sun for a ruling on the status of future greater elemental dragons.<br /> This time, the Unconquered Sun was moved to act, and he decreed that all greater elemental dragons would henceforth be bound until called forth. The Five Elemental Dragons were understandably upset, as they had hoped to find a way to restore the Kukla\u2019s mind, but Gaia acquiesced to the Unconquered Sun\u2019s commandment.&quot; [CoCD, vol 3, pg. 13]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2150-rochedo","name":"Rochedo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2150_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T12:10:52-07:00","id":617911,"title":"","content":"Who was Anisa-Shoshan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T12:40:58-07:00","id":617933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/611354-greater-elemental-dragons-and-why?p=617911#post617911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who was Anisa-Shoshan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anisa-Shoshan, the Maharani of Constellations was the Shogun of Celestial Concerns (pretty much President of Yu-Shan) after their excecution for treason (which was probably a frame job) the position was taken by Ryzala, Lady of Bureaucracy and Paperwork.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 08-06-2015, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T20:21:02-07:00","id":618365,"title":"","content":"Oh I had not considered that... maybe the initial metamorphosis triggers something akin to Limit Break as the GED's sense encompass all of their element in Creation but for whatever reason the Kukla got stuck in a permanent state (possibly due to Sidereal or Celestial sabotage)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T22:43:46-07:00","id":618546,"title":"","content":"The canon says:<br /> Kukla has gone crazy, does not say all GED. Moreover the Elemental Dragons wanted to cure it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2150-rochedo","name":"Rochedo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2150_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T03:31:43-07:00","id":618659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/611354-greater-elemental-dragons-and-why?p=611635#post611635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lesser elemental dragon who ascends to become a greater elemental dragon doesn't &quot;go mad&quot; so much as they cease to be a person, becoming instead an incarnate force of nature. None of the everyday examples of madness are really useful for analogizing that transition.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Goes on violent rampage because a magical switch flicks in their brain&quot; is the everyday example of madness.<br /> <br /> &quot;No longer really a person&quot; is most certainly part of that script.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T03:48:05-07:00","id":618665,"title":"","content":"This is suddenly taking a very uncomfortable turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-i